<title>FRANCE: French Feb unemployment falls 0.2 pct in February.</title>
<headline>French Feb unemployment falls 0.2 pct in February.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The seasonally adjusted number of people unemployed in France in February fell by 7,500, or 0.2 percent, to 3,092,300, the Labour Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>But the jobless rate, based on International Labour Organisation (ILO) criteria, which exclude jobseekers who did any work at all during the month, rose to 12.8 percent from 12.7 percent.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following seasonally adjusted data:</p>
<p>				  end-Feb   month-on-month year-on-year</p>
<p> Jobless rate (ILO)	 12.8 pct   0.1 pctge pt   0.7 pctge pt</p>
<p> Unemployment		3,092,300    -0.2 pct	    2.4 pct</p>
<p> Unemployment (ILO)	3,277,000     0.3 pct	    6.1 pct</p>
<p> Jobs offered		  199,600    -2.6 pct	    6.4 pct</p>
<p> New jobless registrations 370,200    -0.8 pct	   -3.9 pct</p>
<p> Jobless register exits    354,800     2.7 pct	    0.7 pct</p>
</text>
